IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`

-- Part 8 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Chapter 1 (work-related requirements), regulations 84 to 88:
-- the introduction, the terms about carers, the nomination of the responsible carer and the responsible foster parent,
-- the meaning of obtaining paid work, and the expected number of hours per week.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- WHO DECIDES. The "responsible carer" of a child is a concept of the Act (sections 19 to 22) and the nomination of regulation 86
-- says which of joint claimants it is; whether a claimant is one is a stated input. The hours in regulation 88(2) are numbers
-- "that the Secretary of State considers" compatible or reasonable: each is a stated NUMBER input, read only when its limb applies.

§ `Part 8 — Claimant responsibilities`

-- src:1359 | PART 8 — CLAIMANT RESPONSIBILITIES

§§ `Chapter 1 — Work-related requirements`

-- src:1360 | CHAPTER 1 — WORK-RELATED REQUIREMENTS
-- src:1361 | Introductory

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 84 — Introduction`

-- Regulation 84 describes the Chapter and cites sections 15 to 25 of the Act. It states no rule and has no rule in this module
-- (coverage row: inert, a pure citation).
-- src:1362 | 84 Introduction
-- src:1363 | This Chapter contains provisions about the work-related requirements under sections 15 to 25 of the Act, including the persons to whom they are to be applied, the limitations on those requirements and other related matters.
@ref reg 84 (src:1362-1363)
`reg 84 — the Chapter is about the work-related requirements under sections 15 to 25 of the Act` MEANS
        "This Chapter contains provisions about the work-related requirements under sections 15 to 25 of the Act, including the persons to whom they are to be applied, the limitations on those requirements and other related matters."

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 85 — Meaning of terms relating to carers`

-- "relevant carer": (a) a parent of a child who is not the responsible carer for the child but has caring responsibilities for the child,
-- or (b) a person who has caring responsibilities for a person who has a physical or mental impairment.
-- src:1364 | 85 Meaning of terms relating to carers
-- src:1365 | In this Chapter—
-- src:1366 | “relevant carer” means—
-- src:1367 | (a) a parent of a child who is not the responsible carer, but has caring responsibilities for the child; or
-- src:1368 | (b) a person who has caring responsibilities for a person who has a physical or mental impairment; and
@ref reg 85 "relevant carer" (src:1364-1368)
DECLARE `Relevant carer facts` HAS
    `the claimant is a parent of a child`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is the responsible carer for that child`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant has caring responsibilities for that child`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant has caring responsibilities for a person who has a physical or mental impairment`        IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 85 "relevant carer", limb (a) (src:1364-1368)
GIVEN facts IS A `Relevant carer facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 85 — relevant carer, limb (a)` facts MEANS
    (facts's `the claimant is a parent of a child`)
    AND (NOT (facts's `the claimant is the responsible carer for that child`))
    AND (facts's `the claimant has caring responsibilities for that child`)

@ref reg 85 "relevant carer", limb (b) (src:1364-1368)
GIVEN facts IS A `Relevant carer facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 85 — relevant carer, limb (b)` facts MEANS
    facts's `the claimant has caring responsibilities for a person who has a physical or mental impairment`

@ref reg 85 "relevant carer" (src:1364-1368)
GIVEN facts IS A `Relevant carer facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 85 — relevant carer` facts MEANS
    (`reg 85 — relevant carer, limb (a)` facts)
    OR (`reg 85 — relevant carer, limb (b)` facts)

-- "responsible foster parent" in relation to a child: the only foster parent in relation to that child or, where both members of a
-- couple are foster parents in relation to that child, the member nominated under regulation 86. "Foster parent" is the core's
-- `reg 2 — foster parent`, read on each person's placement of the child.
-- src:1369 | “responsible foster parent” in relation to a child means a person who is the only foster parent in relation to that child or, in the case of a couple both members of which are foster parents in relation to that child, the member who is nominated by them in accordance with regulation 86.
@ref reg 85 "responsible foster parent" (src:1369)
DECLARE `Foster parents of a child` HAS
    `the claimant's placement of the child`                                                       IS A `Placement of a child with a person`
    `the other member of the couple's placement of the child`                                     IS A MAYBE `Placement of a child with a person`
    `any other person, not a member of the couple, is a foster parent in relation to the child`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is the member nominated in accordance with regulation 86`                       IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 85 "responsible foster parent" (src:1369)
GIVEN foster IS A `Foster parents of a child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 85 — responsible foster parent` foster MEANS
    `the claimant is a foster parent`
    AND (`the only foster parent` OR (`both members are foster parents` AND (foster's `the claimant is the member nominated in accordance with regulation 86`)))
    WHERE
        `the claimant is a foster parent` MEANS `reg 2 — foster parent` (foster's `the claimant's placement of the child`)
        `the other member is a foster parent` MEANS
            CONSIDER foster's `the other member of the couple's placement of the child`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST placement THEN `reg 2 — foster parent` placement
        `the only foster parent` MEANS
            (NOT `the other member is a foster parent`)
            AND (NOT (foster's `any other person, not a member of the couple, is a foster parent in relation to the child`))
        `both members are foster parents` MEANS `the claimant is a foster parent` AND `the other member is a foster parent`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 86 — Nomination of responsible carer and responsible foster parent`

-- src:1370 | 86 Nomination of responsible carer and responsible foster parent
-- src:1371 | (1) This regulation makes provision for the nomination of the responsible carer or the responsible foster parent in relation to a child.
@ref reg 86(1) (src:1370-1371)
DECLARE `Nominations by joint claimants` HAS
    `the first joint claimant is nominated as a responsible carer`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the first joint claimant is nominated as a responsible foster parent`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the second joint claimant is nominated as a responsible carer`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the second joint claimant is nominated as a responsible foster parent`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- Paragraph (2): only one of joint claimants may be nominated, as a responsible carer or as a responsible foster parent.
-- The rule says whether the nominations made keep within that limit; it does not say that any nomination has been made.
-- src:1372 | (2) Only one of joint claimants may be nominated as a responsible carer or a responsible foster parent.
@ref reg 86(2) (src:1372)
GIVEN nominations IS A `Nominations by joint claimants`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 86(2) — only one of joint claimants is nominated` nominations MEANS
    NOT (`the first is nominated` AND `the second is nominated`)
    WHERE
        `the first is nominated` MEANS
            (nominations's `the first joint claimant is nominated as a responsible carer`)
            OR (nominations's `the first joint claimant is nominated as a responsible foster parent`)
        `the second is nominated` MEANS
            (nominations's `the second joint claimant is nominated as a responsible carer`)
            OR (nominations's `the second joint claimant is nominated as a responsible foster parent`)

-- Paragraph (3): the nomination applies to all the children, where there is more than one, for whom either of the joint claimants
-- is responsible. Children are named by the caller; the rule says a child is covered if either joint claimant is responsible for the child.
-- src:1373 | (3) The nomination applies to all the children, where there is more than one, for whom either of the joint claimants is responsible.
@ref reg 86(3) (src:1373)
GIVEN child IS A STRING
      `children for whom the first joint claimant is responsible` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `children for whom the second joint claimant is responsible` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 86(3) — the nomination applies to a child` child `children for whom the first joint claimant is responsible` `children for whom the second joint claimant is responsible` MEANS
    (elem child `children for whom the first joint claimant is responsible`)
    OR (elem child `children for whom the second joint claimant is responsible`)

-- Paragraph (4): joint claimants may change which member is nominated (a) once in a 12 month period, starting from the date of the
-- previous nomination, or (b) on any occasion where the Secretary of State considers there has been a change of circumstances
-- relevant to the nomination. Limb (a) is read as a limit on how often: a change under (a) is allowed from the day twelve months
-- after the previous nomination (fork F-86-1). Limb (b) is the Secretary of State's judgment, a stated input.
-- src:1374 | (4) Joint claimants may change which member is nominated—
-- src:1375 | (a) once in a 12 month period, starting from the date of the previous nomination; or
-- src:1376 | (b) on any occasion where the Secretary of State considers that there has been a change of circumstances which is relevant to the nomination.
@ref reg 86(4) (src:1374-1376)
GIVEN `date of the previous nomination` IS A DATE
      `date of the change` IS A DATE
      `the Secretary of State considers that there has been a change of circumstances which is relevant to the nomination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 86(4) — the joint claimants may change which member is nominated` `date of the previous nomination` `date of the change` `the Secretary of State considers that there has been a change of circumstances which is relevant to the nomination` MEANS
    `once in a 12 month period starting from the previous nomination`
    OR `the Secretary of State considers that there has been a change of circumstances which is relevant to the nomination`
    WHERE
        `once in a 12 month period starting from the previous nomination` MEANS
            (Day `date of the change` MINUS Day (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` `date of the previous nomination` (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 12, unit IS months))) AT LEAST 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 87 — References to paid work`

-- References in the Chapter to obtaining paid work include obtaining more paid work or better-paid work.
-- src:1377 | 87 References to paid work
-- src:1378 | References in this Chapter to obtaining paid work include obtaining more paid work or better-paid work.
@ref reg 87 (src:1377-1378)
GIVEN `the claimant obtains paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant obtains more paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant obtains better-paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 87 — the claimant obtains paid work, including more or better-paid work` `the claimant obtains paid work` `the claimant obtains more paid work` `the claimant obtains better-paid work` MEANS
    `the claimant obtains paid work`
    OR `the claimant obtains more paid work`
    OR `the claimant obtains better-paid work`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 88 — Expected hours`

-- Paragraph (1): the expected number of hours per week is 35 unless some lesser number applies under paragraph (2).
-- src:1379 | 88 Expected hours
-- src:1380 | (1) The “expected number of hours per week” in relation to a claimant for the purposes of determining their individual threshold in regulation 90 or for the purposes of regulation 95 or 97 is 35 unless some lesser number of hours applies under paragraph (2).
@ref reg 88(1) (src:1379-1380)
`reg 88(1) — the expected number of hours per week, unless a lesser number applies` MEANS 35

-- Paragraph (2): the lesser number is, in each case, a number of hours that the Secretary of State considers compatible or
-- reasonable. The facts and the four numbers are stated inputs; a number is read only when its limb applies.
-- src:1381 | (2) The lesser number of hours is—
-- src:1382 | (a) where—
-- src:1383 | (i) the claimant is a relevant carer, a responsible carer (subject to the following sub-paragraphs) or a responsible foster parent, and
-- src:1384 | (ii) the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work,
-- src:1385 | the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with those caring responsibilities;
-- src:1386 | (aa) where the claimant is a responsible carer of a child who has not yet reached compulsory school age, the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with those caring responsibilities;
-- src:1387 | (b) where the claimant is a responsible carer for a child who has reached compulsory school age but who is under the age of 13, the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with the child's normal school hours (including the normal time it takes the child to travel to and from school); or
-- src:1388 | (c) where the claimant has a physical or mental impairment, the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is reasonable in light of the impairment.
@ref reg 88(2) (src:1381-1388)
DECLARE `Expected hours facts` HAS
    `the claimant is a relevant carer`                                                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is a responsible carer`                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is a responsible foster parent`                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with those caring responsibilities, limb (a)`      IS A NUMBER
    `the claimant is a responsible carer of a child who has not yet reached compulsory school age`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with those caring responsibilities, limb (aa)`     IS A NUMBER
    `the claimant is a responsible carer for a child who has reached compulsory school age but who is under the age of 13`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with the child's normal school hours`              IS A NUMBER
    `the claimant has a physical or mental impairment`                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is reasonable in light of the impairment`                        IS A NUMBER

-- Limb (aa): a responsible carer of a child who has not yet reached compulsory school age.
@ref reg 88(2)(aa) (src:1381-1388)
GIVEN facts IS A `Expected hours facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 88(2)(aa) — the lesser number applies for a responsible carer of a child below compulsory school age` facts MEANS
    (facts's `the claimant is a responsible carer`)
    AND (facts's `the claimant is a responsible carer of a child who has not yet reached compulsory school age`)

-- Limb (b): a responsible carer for a child who has reached compulsory school age but is under 13.
@ref reg 88(2)(b) (src:1381-1388)
GIVEN facts IS A `Expected hours facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 88(2)(b) — the lesser number applies for a responsible carer of a child of compulsory school age under 13` facts MEANS
    (facts's `the claimant is a responsible carer`)
    AND (facts's `the claimant is a responsible carer for a child who has reached compulsory school age but who is under the age of 13`)

-- Limb (a): a relevant carer, a responsible carer "subject to the following sub-paragraphs" or a responsible foster parent, when the
-- Secretary of State is satisfied the claimant has reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work. A responsible carer comes under
-- (a) only where limb (aa) or (b) does not apply to that claimant (fork F-88-2).
@ref reg 88(2)(a) (src:1381-1388)
GIVEN facts IS A `Expected hours facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 88(2)(a) — the lesser number applies for a carer or foster parent with reasonable prospects of work` facts MEANS
    `a person described in (i)`
    AND (facts's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has reasonable prospects of obtaining paid work`)
    WHERE
        `a person described in (i)` MEANS
            (facts's `the claimant is a relevant carer`)
            OR `a responsible carer not under limb (aa) or (b)`
            OR (facts's `the claimant is a responsible foster parent`)
        `a responsible carer not under limb (aa) or (b)` MEANS
            (facts's `the claimant is a responsible carer`)
            AND (NOT (`reg 88(2)(aa) — the lesser number applies for a responsible carer of a child below compulsory school age` facts))
            AND (NOT (`reg 88(2)(b) — the lesser number applies for a responsible carer of a child of compulsory school age under 13` facts))

-- Limb (c): the claimant has a physical or mental impairment.
@ref reg 88(2)(c) (src:1381-1388)
GIVEN facts IS A `Expected hours facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 88(2)(c) — the lesser number applies for a claimant with an impairment` facts MEANS
    facts's `the claimant has a physical or mental impairment`

-- The expected number of hours: 35, or the least of the numbers of the limbs that apply (and never more than 35, because only
-- a "lesser" number applies). If several limbs apply the text does not say which governs; the least is taken (fork F-88-1).
@ref reg 88(1) and (2) (src:1379-1388)
GIVEN facts IS A `Expected hours facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 88 — the expected number of hours per week` facts MEANS
    minimum (LIST 35, `limb (a) number`, `limb (aa) number`, `limb (b) number`, `limb (c) number`)
    WHERE
        `limb (a) number` MEANS
            IF `reg 88(2)(a) — the lesser number applies for a carer or foster parent with reasonable prospects of work` facts
            THEN facts's `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with those caring responsibilities, limb (a)`
            ELSE 35
        `limb (aa) number` MEANS
            IF `reg 88(2)(aa) — the lesser number applies for a responsible carer of a child below compulsory school age` facts
            THEN facts's `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with those caring responsibilities, limb (aa)`
            ELSE 35
        `limb (b) number` MEANS
            IF `reg 88(2)(b) — the lesser number applies for a responsible carer of a child of compulsory school age under 13` facts
            THEN facts's `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is compatible with the child's normal school hours`
            ELSE 35
        `limb (c) number` MEANS
            IF `reg 88(2)(c) — the lesser number applies for a claimant with an impairment` facts
            THEN facts's `the number of hours that the Secretary of State considers is reasonable in light of the impairment`
            ELSE 35
